{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Ban restrictive covenants from preventing AED installations on private property",
        "additional_details": "We therefore call on the Government to legislate to ban all existing and future restrictive covenants from preventing AED installations on private property.\r\n\r\nIn many rural and urban parts of the country, ambulance response times are some of the worst in the UK. The nearest AED may be at best a 14 mins roundtrip drive, making it an impossible lifesaving exercise. If you are a couple, you may have to make a decision of staying with your partner or going to get help. We believe it would be unfair to leave your unresponsive loved one unattended for 14 mins, and that more AED installations could reduce that to 3 or 4 mins and allow us to save lives.",
        "background": "We believe that if a housing estate has amenity land, then it should be possible to install a 100 x 100cm concrete base for an AED installation (K6 phone box etc) to be erected where transfer deeds prohibit but where residents agree the need & siting on the amenity land.",
